  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Daulat Singh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 10 September, 2024 Author: Dinesh Kumar Paliwal Bench: Dinesh Kumar Paliwal 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Crr No. 4402 of 2022 (Daulat Singh Vs The State Of Madhya Prades Dated : 10-09-2024 Shri Sankalp Kochar - Advocate for the applicant. Shri Aditya Gupta - Panel Lawyer for the respondent/Stat",
    "facts": "It is revision, therefore, provision of Section 389(1) of Cr.P.C and Section 430 of BNSS are not applicable.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant has been erroneously convicted by both the Courts below as they have not taken into consideration the fact that on the date on which the offence alleged to have been committed Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 was not in force, the same has already been repealed by Food Safety Standard Act, 2006. Therefore, it was not justified for the Courts below to convict the applicant under the provisions of the repealed Act. He has fair chances Daulat Singh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 10 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/62855944/ 1 to succeed in revision. It is further contended that the applicant is 78 years old man and on account of old age related infirmities and problems it has become difficult for him to survive. Therefore, it is prayed that the jail sentence of applicant may be suspended and he may be released on bail, till final hearing in revision. On the other hand, learned counsel appearing for the State has opposed grant of bail and suspension of jail sentence.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant has been erroneously convicted by both the Courts below as they have not taken into consideration the fact that on the date on which the offence alleged to have been committed Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 was not in force, the same has already been repealed by Food Safety Standard Act, 2006. Therefore, it was not justified for the Courts below to convict the applicant under the provisions of the repealed Act. He has fair chances Daulat Singh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 10 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/62855944/ 1 to succeed in revision. It is further contended that the applicant is 78 years old man and on account of old age related infirmities and problems it has become difficult for him to survive. Therefore, it is prayed that the jail sentence of applicant may be suspended and he may be released on bail, till final hearing in revision. On the other hand, learned counsel appearing for the State has opposed grant of bail and suspension of jail sentence.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
